## Summary

Audited the codebase for structural simplifications and made one focused cleanup in `internal/tools/calendar.go`.

Before: calendar event household attribution used an audience-to-event reverse map and a second map of matching events.
Now: each event checks its own ID and audience reference directly against the existing membership set.

Before: RSVP attribution mapped answer groups to event IDs and rescanned every event for each membership.
Now: answer groups map directly to event rows, removing the nested scan.

Kept policy-filtered queries and output shape unchanged. Left ancestry consolidation alone because query traversal could alter handling of unreadable parents; left feed and invitation span handling separate because their missing-end and all-day rules differ.

The requested `git merge --no-ff --no-commit main` reported already up to date; no conflicts or additional changes were needed. The full `internal/tools` tests, repository-wide `go vet`, and diff checks passed.

